# behavior: Inline comments stay on their statement, conditionals and loops receive canonical spacing, long for, if let and match headers wrap into parseable grouped layouts, a long and/or header puts one operand per line inside parentheses, with a nested group on one line when it fits and in its own block when it does not, and a long and/or assignment or return value takes the same parenthesized layout rather than breaking an operand's method chain (#2589).
